Give winemac.drv's five translator entry points default visibility.

Wine builds its Unix libraries with hidden visibility, so winemac.so exports
only its two unix-call tables: this project's Wine 11.0 build has 2 exported
symbols out of 1905 entries. An independently sourced Direct3D-to-Metal
translator resolves entry points from the loaded driver by name, which cannot
work while they are local symbols.

Audited against DXMT revision e94c312f5c054263acf261cfa109edf13e757587, its unix
layer first looks for a `macdrv_functions` structure, which is a CrossOver export
absent from upstream Wine, and otherwise resolves exactly these five by name:
get_win_data, release_win_data, macdrv_view_create_metal_view,
macdrv_view_get_metal_layer and macdrv_view_release_metal_view. The other names
in that structure, including macdrv_create_metal_device and
macdrv_get_cocoa_window, are never looked up on the upstream path, so they are
deliberately left local.

This changes no behaviour on its own: it widens linkage for existing functions
and adds, removes and renames nothing. Measured against this project's Wine 11.0
build, winemac.so goes from 2 exported symbols to 7.

Applies to Wine 11.0. Upstream Wine is LGPL-2.1-or-later; this patch is offered
under the same terms.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv.h
@@ -206,8 +206,8 @@
 
 extern struct macdrv_client_surface *macdrv_client_surface_create(HWND hwnd);
 
-extern struct macdrv_win_data *get_win_data(HWND hwnd);
-extern void release_win_data(struct macdrv_win_data *data);
+__attribute__((visibility("default"))) extern struct macdrv_win_data *get_win_data(HWND hwnd);
+__attribute__((visibility("default"))) extern void release_win_data(struct macdrv_win_data *data);
 extern void init_win_context(void);
 extern macdrv_window macdrv_get_cocoa_window(HWND hwnd, BOOL require_on_screen);
 extern RGNDATA *get_region_data(HRGN hrgn, HDC hdc_lptodp);
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h
@@ -524,9 +524,9 @@
 extern void macdrv_remove_view_opengl_context(macdrv_view v, macdrv_opengl_context c);
 extern macdrv_metal_device macdrv_create_metal_device(void);
 extern void macdrv_release_metal_device(macdrv_metal_device d);
-extern macdrv_metal_view macdrv_view_create_metal_view(macdrv_view v, macdrv_metal_device d);
-extern macdrv_metal_layer macdrv_view_get_metal_layer(macdrv_metal_view v);
-extern void macdrv_view_release_metal_view(macdrv_metal_view v);
+__attribute__((visibility("default"))) extern macdrv_metal_view macdrv_view_create_metal_view(macdrv_view v, macdrv_metal_device d);
+__attribute__((visibility("default"))) extern macdrv_metal_layer macdrv_view_get_metal_layer(macdrv_metal_view v);
+__attribute__((visibility("default"))) extern void macdrv_view_release_metal_view(macdrv_metal_view v);
 extern bool macdrv_get_view_backing_size(macdrv_view v, int backing_size[2]);
 extern void macdrv_set_view_backing_size(macdrv_view v, const int backing_size[2]);
 extern uint32_t macdrv_window_background_color(void);
